SM(524,{"n":"Romans 14","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Romans 14.mp3","d":2205.7,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.96,"Okay, so chapter 14, verse one."],[27.2,"Receive one who is weak in the faith, but not to disputes over doubtful things."],[33.12,"So we all are at different stages in the Christian life."],[40.0,"We're all, regardless of our physical age, we also have sort of a spiritual maturity level."],[48.48,"There's some people who are very advanced in age who are not very advanced spiritually."],[52.32,"There are some people who are very young in age who are very advanced spiritually."],[58.08,"So these are disassociated."],[59.88,"And so St."],[60.68,"Paul here is referring to someone who's weak in this case is someone who is immature spiritually."],[66.44,"Okay. And he's saying you need to receive that kind of person."],[70.06,"You don't push that person off because they don't understand and they don't, you know, aren't necessarily on board with everything you're doing, or they ask too many questions, or whatever."],[79.26,"He says, but but what you do not do with that person is engage in disputes over doubtful things."],[87.5,"You don't receive them so that they can argue about everything."],[91.82,"That's not the purpose."],[92.94,"The purpose of receiving them is so that hopefully they can begin to grow toward greater maturity and understanding."],[100.38,"I notice in reading reading fathers or ascetics or whatever, is that theological disputes play very little role in anything they write."],[115.47,"And you find with generally with the the even with the church fathers who engaged in theological controversies, they're focused on very key important things."],[128.75,"And things that are a crisis at the moment."],[131.64,"Things that are a crisis right now and things that cut to the heart of salvation."],[135.14,"If someone comes along and says Jesus isn't God, well, that kind of cuts to the heart of the gospel."],[140.28,"And we have to say something about that."],[142.0,"But if somebody shows up and says, you know, I think it's okay to eat alligator on a fast day, I think it should count as as fish and not as uh, you know, meat, that's not something we find the fathers spending a lot of time about."],[159.9,"The details of the fasting rules."],[161.98,"Or as we would find the rabbis spending a lot of time on those."],[166.3,"Spending a lot of time on those things and internet message boards."],[169.5,"Spending a lot of times on those things."],[171.34,"But most of the people who are on those message boards debating those things are not the most spiritually mature people in the church."],[177.98,"It's not the bishops."],[179.51,"Going and posting on a message board and arguing about fasting rules."],[183.64,"And so he's saying, receive them, but this is not why we're receiving them."],[188.2,"So just to point out, because I I'm pointing out something you often point out, uh, weak in the faith."],[195.44,"That doesn't mean somebody who is not believing hard enough."],[201.12,"Not believing hard enough."],[202.56,"Which doesn't make any sense anyway."],[204.88,"Isn't uh doesn't understand uh quite what how the the Eucharist works, uh something like that."],[215.14,"This is a person who is not sort of their Christian life is not mature and robust."],[220.98,"They're still sort of figuring things out."],[223.46,"This is a constant problem I have."],[226.18,"I don't know, it's not my problem."],[227.7,"Uh it's Gail's problem."],[229.22,"Um she I would say that the biggest reason she hasn't come into orthodoxy is that she's afraid that she'll be asked to believe something that she isn't convinced of in a logical sense, in a rational sense."],[247.34,"She wants all the answers before she'll commit."],[252.94,"And in the Episcopal Church, this works well."],[257.18,"Yeah. Uh and uh in the Orthodox Church, it shouldn't be an issue."],[263.71,"But she doesn't understand that."],[265.63,"Yeah. Yeah. Challenging me on theological minutiae"],[272.43,"Yeah. And I usually say, I don't know."],[275.95,"I say a lot in the catechumen classs. that there' only one reason why you should join the Orthodox Church"],[285.35,"And that's that you've come here and you've discovered that Christ is here."],[290.31,"If you haven't had that experience, you shouldn't join."],[293.51,"You should keep looking until you find Christ."],[296.47,"And if you've come here and you found Christ here, if Christ is here, then whatever was being taught here, whatever's being sung here, however he's being worshipped here, if he's here, then that's where the that obedience uh part kicks in."],[313.96,"Because obedience isn't just physical terms of our actions, it's in terms of our intellect as well."],[320.76,"And it requires the same kind of intellectual humility."],[324.13,"You know, I don't understand this, but that doesn't mean it isn't true."],[329.74,"And and if Christ is here, this is where he's being worshipped."],[333.34,"And I don't know about some of this stuff they say about the Theotokos."],[339.1,"I don't know if I'm comfortable with that yet."],[341.74,"But I do know that Christ is here."],[344.78,"I do know this is the place where I find him."],[347.5,"And so I'll understand that at some point."],[350.62,"This is we we're quoting Saint Augustine tonight, so I believe so that I may understand."],[357.02,"Um that yeah, that that's that's been my experience a lot because um my conversion to Christianity. was really an experience"],[372.5,"And I said, okay, I have previously thrown out all of these ideas because they didn't make sense."],[381.7,"Now I know that I have to accept them and perhaps they'll they will make sense eventually."],[388.9,"And so you know, as I've lived these last 50 years or so, and so I've been, oh yeah, okay, that now I understand that."],[397.78,"And there's plenty left that I don't understand yet."],[400.74,"But but I'm I'm committed, so uh but I don't understand I I don't want I don't want to say I'm just a take on faith."],[411.46,"Yeah I take on obedience it on."],[411.58,"I take on obedience."],[412.58,"Yeah It's it's that humility of accepting."],[421.16,"I don't understand."],[422.44,"Because I don't understand something, that doesn't mean it makes no sense."],[425.56,"Yeah. Otherwise, that just means I don't understand."],[429.38,"It just means I don't understand."],[430.82,"Yeah. Uh-huh. It may very well be true."],[433.88,"I just don't get it yet."],[436.68,"Um Yeah. So that that that concept is is important."],[443.88,"That concept is important."],[445.64,"And that's why there there are a lot of there are a lot of discussions, theological discussions like that, like about my new show, like you mentioned, that I will tell people I don't think are really I'll tell them politely, but people who aren't Orthodox, I'll tell them they're they're really not worth having."],[466.08,"For example, a friend of mine who's who's Protestant wanted to talk to me about closed communion, about the fact that we don't give the Eucharist to non Orthodox people."],[478.8,"Um and I I basically said, well, to understand why we don't do that, you'd have to accept all the things we believe and experience about the Eucharist and all of these other things."],[492.82,"I can't just discuss this issue with you."],[497.22,"Yeah, it's not off by itself as this discrete point."],[501.3,"It's part of this whole lived experience of the Eucharist and the liturgy and the Orthodox Christian life"],[507.1,"And so I can't really debate it with you from the outside to try and convince you it's true."],[515.63,"Without all the rest."],[517.31,"So he goes on to give some examples."],[519.07,"He says, For one who believes he may eat all things, but he who is weak eats only vegetables."],[526.11,"What is he referring to here?"],[528.03,"Well very bad sentence."],[530.75,"Yeah, they added uh a word or two and it didn't help much."],[534.59,"But um the idea is that there's someone."],[537.25,"There's someone in your community who believes I can eat whatever I want."],[541.17,"Uh-huh. Meaning Jewish food rules don't apply."],[545.61,"Uh-huh. I'm not even super worried about the fact that some meat I pick up at the meat market might have somewhere been involved in a sacrifice because I'm not going to the temple and I'm not involved in the sacrifice."],[556.99,"And so I eat it, I give thanks to God for it."],[562.27,"It's all good."],[564.05,"You have another person who's who's a weaker person, who's newer in the faith, um, who takes the approach that this eating only vegetables, that's what Daniel and his friends did in the book of Daniel when they were in Babylon because they didn't want to eat any meat that might have been offered to idols."],[582.47,"So this person says, maybe they're a former pagan, uh huh."],[586.4,"Maybe they they''rere they're uh Jewish and still holding on to some of those traditions."],[591.72,"For whatever reason, they say, I'm only gonna eat vegetables."],[595.32,"You have these two people who have these two different ways of life regarding eating in your community."],[600.04,"At first glance, the vegetarian seems like the strong one, not the weak one."],[606.52,"Because he's disciplining himself."],[609.24,"He's not right."],[610.92,"So Rebecca weak here is referring to spiritual maturity."],[614.14,"Well, why is it so spiritually mature to say I can eat anything?"],[619.74,"Because it reflects a greater understanding of, for example, the purpose of the food laws in the Old Testament."],[626.58,"And the way that that Christ has taken away uncleanness from the physical world."],[632.46,"Right? There's there's theological teachings in the Christian community"],[639.38,"That are involved in his being able to say that."],[642.12,"I see. He's not saying it just because he doesn't care."],[647.24,"He doesn't want to follow rules."],[648.44,"Yeah, he doesn't want to follow rules."],[650.06,"So he's he's come to this conclusion through his understanding of the material world and who Christ is and what he's done and how that relates to the Torah and how that relates to meat offered to idols."],[662.38,"So there's a whole series of things here that your new your new convert may not understand."],[668.86,"Your new convert is going, Oh, I shouldn't eat any meat offered to idols."],[674.14,"Uh huh. And some of that meat in the meat market might be offered to idols."],[677.34,"So I better not eat any at all"],[679.7,"Right? Or I'm not sure why we keep some parts of the Torah, but we're not keeping the kosher rules."],[686.74,"So I better keep kosher."],[690.26,"So this person doesn't have a thoroughly evolved understanding yet."],[695.06,"Okay. So this isn't the weak person who's causing disputes."],[698.6,"So this isn't like someone showing up and trying to argue."],[701.16,"Everyone here has to follow the food."],[704.76,"That's a different category."],[706.36,"This is just a person who for his own, this is part of what I mentioned when we're going to get to conscience."],[711.64,"This person for their own their own selves, they think it's not, I shouldn't do this."],[716.52,"Yeah. Whereas this other person is more confident and mature in their faith and says, hey. you know, this is how I approach it"],[725.77,"Let not him who eats despise him who does not eat, and let not him who does not eat judge him who eats, for God has received him."],[735.13,"Who are you to judge another's servant?"],[737.53,"To his own master he stands or falls."],[740.09,"Indeed, he will be made to stand, for God is able to make him stand."],[744.81,"Okay, so he's saying, on one hand, the person who eats whatever shouldn't look at this person who only eats vegetables and be like, you ignoramus."],[755.36,"Oh, yeah, little faith."],[757.29,"And uh disdain him."],[759.05,"On the other hand, the one who only eats vegetables shouldn't be judging this person who he oh, did you see he bought some meat at the meat market?"],[763.79,"And and judge him"],[766.87,"I bet that was, you know."],[771.11,"And what's the reason why?"],[772.79,"What's important here is St."],[774.31,"Paul's argument why."],[776.47,"People tend to focus on that because their whole focus is on, you know, I think it's okay for me to watch this TV show."],[785.43,"Other people in my church don't think it's okay, and I want to tell them they need to shut up, so I'm gonna quote St."],[790.07,"Paul. Yeah. So but uh but what's important here is is St."],[797.84,"Paul's reason. St."],[799.28,"Paul's reasoning is who are you to judge another servant?"],[803.52,"To his own master, he stands or falls."],[805.68,"Indeed, he'll be made to stand for God is able to make him to stand."],[808.68,"So both of you are servants of Christ."],[812.28,"If you have two people who are servants, if you have two people who are slaves in a household, if you have two employees at a business, it's not their job to evaluate each other's job performance."],[827.32,"Yeah. It's the person they're serving, it's their boss, it's their manager."],[832.84,"It's it's who they're serving, their master."],[835.16,"That's who looks at each of them and evaluates and evaluates them."],[840.94,"So Christ is going to evaluate both of you."],[845.16,"Based on based on what you do."],[848.12,"Um and so you you he's not interested. in your opinions about each other"],[854.96,"You need to focus on serving faith as faithfully as you as you yourself are able."],[860.4,"Now he gives some more examples."],[861.92,"One person esteems one day above another, another esteems every day alike."],[866.64,"Let each be fully convinced in his own mind."],[869.68,"He who observes the day observes it to the Lord, and he who does not observe the day, to the Lord he does not observe it."],[875.6,"He who eats eats to the Lord, for he gives God thanks."],[878.8,"And he who does not eat to the Lord, he does not eat and gives God thanks."],[885.12,"So when he's talking about observing a day, he's talking about the Sabbath."],[888.8,"Sure. The Jewish Sabbath."],[890.11,"He says, so some people still observe that."],[893.41,"And he says, the ones who observe that that,'s a day they're observing for the Lord."],[895.33,"So they're doing a good thing"],[900.47,"And the one who doesn't observe the Jewish Sabbath as a special day, is still going to be giving that day to the Lord, probably in a different way."],[911.16,"And so probably doing it because he he feels that theologically this is fulfilled."],[920.28,"This is fulfilled."],[921.21,"And so and God will evaluate how well each of them has done at honoring the Lord in their own way."],[928.77,"And he says that the one who the one who eats, he gives thanks for that food to God."],[933.84,"So he's giving glory to God."],[935.76,"And the one who doesn't eat is not eating because they're trying to be obedient to God."],[941.74,"And God will honor that."],[943.98,"Uh-huh. For none of us lives to himself, and no one dies to himself."],[948.86,"For if we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord."],[952.86,"Therefore, whether we live or die, we are the Lord's."],[963.74,"You have to serve somebody, to quote Bob Dylan."],[967.5,"You gotta serve somebody."],[969.02,"But you're gonna be you're gonna be serving somebody."],[972.8,"And you're serving the Lord."],[975.12,"Now notice here, he doesn't give another option."],[978.4,"No, he doesn't."],[980.36,"Because he's writing you're all serving the Lord."],[982.92,"Uh-huh. And you're about to say because he's writing to the church."],[986.12,"I was. But I'm about to question that."],[988.2,"Yeah, then I'm not sure."],[991.8,"Because he's gonna drop a little theology on us here."],[994.12,"It's gonna sneak back in."],[996.12,"That's here to the practical section."],[998.6,"For to this end, Christ died and rose and lived again, that he might be Lord of both the dead and the living."],[1006.52,"Okay. Well, what does that have to do with anything?"],[1010.7,"This seems like a weird argument."],[1011.9,"If we die, we die to the lives, oh, and he died and rose again and lived."],[1016.5,"He says basically, there's no escaping service to the Lord."],[1021.74,"Now. He's saying that this is why Christ died."],[1025.91,"Christ dying and rising again made it so that there is no escaping serving the Lord."],[1032.81,"That's that's that's the flow of his argument."],[1035.37,"Why did that require him to to die?"],[1039.69,"Before Christ died, who was the Lord of the dead?"],[1044.25,"Satan. The devil."],[1045.95,"And that's going all the way back to Genesis three."],[1049.56,"We read uh Genesis three in a goofy way, a lot of times in the modern world."],[1055.4,"We read it as, you know, Rudyard Kipling's Just So story about how the snake lost its legs."],[1061.03,"Which is not at all what it's about."],[1063.11,"When it says he's thrown down to the ground, the word the word errets there is actually used for the underworld quite a bit."],[1067.35,"The ancient world"],[1071.23,"He's sort of down to the underworld where it says that he's going to eat dust for the rest of his life."],[1076.35,"Ancient people knew full well that snakes don't eat dirt."],[1079.31,"They'd seen the meat frogs, they'd seen the meat mice and rats."],[1085.15,"That dust is the dust that Adam's going to return to."],[1089.23,"In that very same chapter."],[1092.03,"So what's happening there in that curse is the devil is being cast down into the underworld to be the Lord of the dead."],[1098.91,"So that's his punishment."],[1101.87,"Who knew? That's his punishment."],[1104.75,"Uh-huh Is that he's he's given this kingdom of ashes and dust for trying to us.urp uh God's kingdom"],[1116.63,"Um so he's thrown down the ground, and this is why, for example, in Hebrews it refers to the devil as the one who hold who held the power of death, past tense."],[1127.49,"And so when Christ dies, this is the whole our whole concept of the harrowing of Hades, is that Christ goes and binds him and takes away even that authority that he had and plunders all the people."],[1143.43,"Right. And this is why we have this sort of universal sounding language that we use at Posca."],[1149.33,"Not one dead remains in the graves."],[1152.63,"Not one remains in the devil's realm."],[1155.03,"Everyone is now under Christ's authority"],[1155.63,"No one remains under his authority anymore."],[1161.76,"That's why Christ is going to return to judge the living and the dead."],[1166.38,"Everyone is now under Christ's authority."],[1169.34,"Because, as St."],[1171.02,"Paul says, because he died and rose and lived."],[1175.34,"So he's now the Lord of the living and the dead."],[1177.18,"Everyone who's ever lived is Christ is their Lord and Master."],[1182.78,"And whether so whether they acknowledge it currently or not, whether they uh whether they believe it currently or not, he is their Lord and their master, and the one to whom they will have to give give an account on the day of judgment."],[1199.62,"So this extends not only to your fellow members of the Christian community, but to every human being who you meet."],[1207.4,"And every human being there's ever been or ever will be."],[1210.38,"And so preaching the gospel to them is telling them this truth that Christ has died and rose and lives and ascended into heaven, where he sits enthroned and he's returning to judge the living and the dead, so that they can now choose to live their lives in relationship to that fact."],[1230.88,"Or the fact that he is their Lord."],[1234.08,"We don't get to vote."],[1238.16,"So St. Paul makes this point."],[1240.8,"But why do you judge? your brother, or why do you show contempt for your brother"],[1244.76,"For we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ."],[1249.16,"Every one of us is going to give an account to him."],[1253.96,"So you don't have to account for your actions to me."],[1257.72,"I don't have to account for my actions to you."],[1260.28,"We both have to account for our words and deeds and thoughts to Christ, who is our who is our master."],[1269.48,"For it is written, as I live, says the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God."],[1277.08,"That's Isaiah 45, 23."],[1279.96,"And the Lord there, you see, it's in all caps, that's because it's Yahweh."],[1283.64,"As I live, says Yahweh, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God."],[1286.84,"Now you may have heard something very similar in another context"],[1293.28,"And it's from Philippians chapter 2, where St."],[1297.84,"Paul says, I believe it's verse 13."],[1302.16,"There's a verse 10."],[1303.92,"It's right in there."],[1306.48,"Where uh Saint Paul says, Every knee shall bow and every tongue shall confess that Jesus Christ is Lord."],[1314.96,"Where he repurposes this."],[1316.88,"Uh-huh. So he's saying that Jesus Christ is Yahweh."],[1321.44,"Yes. Uh-huh Yes."],[1323.84,"And that's made even clearer by the fact that in Philippians, when he quotes it, he says, so no, that Jesus Christ is Lord to the glory of God the Father."],[1331.36,"Uh-huh. Meaning he hasn't sort of displaced God the Father or the God of the Old Testament"],[1338.89,"But that the two are one."],[1341.53,"Uh-huh. So yes, this is yet another place where St."],[1345.13,"Paul makes it pretty clear that Christ is Yahweh."],[1349.77,"Um speaking prophetically of that day which will come when everyone will acknowledge the fact that is a fact that uh Christ is their is their Lord."],[1367.61,"Everyone will acknowledge it, I suppose."],[1371.61,"You know, when when Christ comes again."],[1374.89,"that And speaking prophetically of that as he says, said right before, we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ."],[1382.01,"When we find ourselves there, we'll know that that's true."],[1385.11,"Whether we wanted to accept it or not."],[1386.71,"And then it will be revealed what kind of servant we were for him."],[1395.11,"So then each of us shall give account of himself to God."],[1400.23,"Therefore, let us not judge one another anymore, but rather resolve this not to put a stumbling block or a cause to fall in our brother's way."],[1408.95,"So he's talking, he's going to speak now very practically about again how we show love to our brother"],[1416.39,"We had the negative."],[1417.55,"'re not shooting we We shouldn't be judging, evaluating, condemning our brother."],[1420.47,"Or not doing"],[1422.67,"What should we be doing?"],[1426.6,"How does how do we concretely show that love as the alternative?"],[1434.04,"And the way he's going to talk about is not putting a stumbling block or a cause to fall in our brother's path."],[1440.68,"So that would mean not leading him into a temptation."],[1444.97,"So because he's going to stand before Christ, and because I'm serving Christ, it's my job to help him do a better job of serving Christ."],[1458.87,"By me helping him serve Christ, I'm serving Christ."],[1463.75,"Those two go together."],[1464.31,"Paul speaking I know and am convinced, this is St."],[1471.31,"I know, St."],[1472.03,"Paul knows, and I'm convinced by the Lord Jesus that there is nothing unclean of itself."],[1477.55,"But to him who considers anything to be unclean, to him it is unclean."],[1482.91,"So he's saying, look, in and of itself, and we talked about this back in Acts, the way Christ is cleansed and purified the material world."],[1491.71,"So there aren't sort of unclean foods now."],[1494.59,"He says, St."],[1495.55,"Paul says, I'm convinced."],[1497.07,"He's now setting himself up as in the position of that more spiritually mature person."],[1501.55,"I'm convinced There's nothing that in and of itself is unclean to eat."],[1507.13,"But if someone believes it is, if someone honestly believes that for me to eat this would be a sin against God and so I shouldn't eat it."],[1518.03,"Then for him to act in what he thinks is disobedience, even if God hasn't really given that commandment."],[1525.77,"If he believes that, then for him to be disobedient to that, for him it's going to be a sin because of his attitude."],[1533.78,"In his heart."],[1536.26,"Yet if your brother is grieved because of your food, you are no longer walking in love."],[1541.38,"Do not destroy with your food the one for whom Christ died."],[1545.4,"So I have this freedom."],[1547.42,"I understand all this theologically."],[1550.14,"I I can can go and eat right at the local Chinese restaurant."],[1555.86,"I don't have to worry if they lit incense while they were cooking the Chinese food."],[1563.0,"I could eat pork, I could eat whatever."],[1565.9,"I'll say that I'll say thanks to God for it."],[1568.54,"But if there's someone else who's going to see me doing that."],[1577.66,"Not offended by it."],[1579.74,"Who's going to be caused the it's going to cause them to offend."],[1584.47,"Meaning they're going to see me do it and say, Oh, I see that."],[1586.87,"Oh, you're going to be able to do it."],[1587.59,"Well. And follow my example."],[1589.85,"And that's going to lead them down the wrong road."],[1594.01,"So the the case is a case where somebody said believes this is wrong, sees you do it, and says, okay, it's wrong, but I guess he gets away with it, so I guess I can."],[1606.35,"And then once they've broken their conscience on that, maybe they start breaking it on other things."],[1611.88,"Which we would all agree are really wrong."],[1614.94,"And so they start, they move from the path of trying to be obedient to not caring."],[1619.98,"They become more lax."],[1621.87,"And so this is where St."],[1623.55,"Paul says, you know, uh, do not destroy with your food the one for whom Christ died."],[1630.13,"Christ loved this person so much to die for them."],[1632.93,"And you don't even care enough about them to not eat a ham sandwich for. lunch, to get roast beef instead"],[1641.11,"That seems to be a very minimal definition of sort of love and compassion."],[1648.39,"Therefore do not let your good be spoken of as evil, for the kingdom of God is not eating and drinking, but righteousness and peace and joy in the Holy Spirit."],[1658.09,"These are the things we're after in life, not eating and drinking and having a good time and enjoying ourselves."],[1666.41,"For he who serves Christ in these things is acceptable to God and approved by men."],[1672.41,"Therefore, let us pursue the things which make for peace and the things by which one may edify another."],[1677.85,"Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food."],[1680.81,"All things indeed are pure, but it is evil for the man who eats with offense."],[1685.73,"It is good neither to eat meat, nor drink wine, nor do anything by which your brother stumbles or is offended or is made weak."],[1694.85,"So the the drinking wine there is a good is, I think, a better or more modern contemporary example."],[1702.37,"Yeah. I may be able to enjoy an adult beverage or two now and then, you know, and not have any issue."],[1709.95,"You know. There are plenty of people in the world who can't."],[1714.99,"Yeah. And so if seeing me, especially as a clergy person, do that leads them down a wrong road, it's better for me to just say, you know what?"],[1725.31,"I can drink a Diet Coke."],[1727.11,"Uh-huh. You know?"],[1730.63,"And so this is about love."],[1733.43,"This would apply also if you're if you're out with a bunch of Baptists, don't order, don't order a martini."],[1744.17,"There's no there's no reason to."],[1746.63,"And so this is talking about St."],[1748.87,"Paul's already been clear we don't make provision to our sinful desires."],[1755.03,"But he's saying even our non sinful desires, we should be willing to sacrifice for better things."],[1764.25,"For better things."],[1765.77,"And this is really the the basis of asceticism."],[1770.63,"Asceticism isn't giving up sin."],[1773.6,"We're always supposed to give up sin."],[1777.68,"Asceticism is getting up giving up good things in order to get better things."],[1789.69,"If there was, we wouldn't eat chicken the rest of the year."],[1793.77,"But we give up having a full belly and spending money on entertainment and those kind of things during Lent because we want to focus on other things that are more important and that are better."],[1808.09,"And that's the same thing St."],[1809.53,"Paul is arguing we should do all the time in terms of our love for each other within the community."],[1817.25,"The question isn't is what I'm about to do a sin or not, technically."],[1820.93,"Uh-huh. This is getting back to the rules versus love."],[1824.79,"The question is, is me doing this showing love for my neighbor?"],[1831.25,"And going back to the alcohol examples, there might be cases where it is."],[1835.01,"If I go to somebody's house and it's just me and them in the privacy of their home and they offer me a drink, you know, and me sitting and sharing that drink with them and talking with them may be an expression of love for them and fellowship and brotherhood for Christ."],[1851.95,"Whereas it in the home of a recovering alcoholic, it would be quite different."],[1854.83,"be Or me cracking open aer in the youth group."],[1861.88,"Um so yes, so this is what St."],[1864.12,"Paul is calling on us to do, to be willing to out of love, give up our freedoms."],[1872.5,"Give up our rights."],[1874.42,"We are very much as modern American people concerned about our rights."],[1877.94,"I have the right to do this and the right to do that if I want to, and and you can't tell me I can't, and that and St."],[1884.5,"Paul is again charting the opposite course."],[1888.79,"That uh we're responsible for doing good and loving each other and bringing about peace."],[1897.59,"Um, those things are more important than my rights"],[1901.47,"And if I have to give up some of my rights in order to get those other things, then that's a good trade."],[1908.03,"Um it's a trade that I need to make."],[1912.83,"He says, Do you have faith?"],[1914.67,"Have it to yourself before God."],[1916.43,"Happy is he who does not condemn himself in what he approves."],[1920.11,"But he who doubts is condemned if he eats, because he does not eat from faith."],[1924.43,"For whatever is not from faith is sin."],[1927.71,"Okay, you're gonna straighten that one out."],[1929.55,"Yeah. So you have faith, you're mature."],[1935.85,"You're spiritually mature."],[1937.67,"So you know that these things are fine, you know, there's no that you could do this or that. in moderation"],[1944.35,"You're mature enough to know what moderation is and what you could do."],[1950.27,"And he says, you know, great."],[1953.64,"Between you and God, that's great."],[1957.98,"And you will be at the head to yourself before God."],[1961.88,"And you will you will be happy in your life."],[1967.25,"Because you know, you have this understanding."],[1971.23,"So you will have things that you enjoy in life that someone who's weaker may never get to enjoy because they're not at that level where they can do it responsibly."],[1982.19,"But he who doubts is condemned if he eats because he does not eat from faith."],[1986.24,"Meaning the person who doesn't understand or doesn't even think that it's okay."],[1994.1,"Who thinks that this is wrong, but then does it anyway."],[1998.18,"Yeah. Well, anytime anytime you say this is wrong and I'm going to do it anyway, you know you're a sinner."],[2005.56,"And so he's saying for that person."],[2008.52,"Yeah. And so remember, faith we can translate as faithfulness."],[2013.95,"Yeah, that helps."],[2015.07,"He's not eating out of faithfulness or obedience to God."],[2018.59,"Quite the opposite."],[2019.47,"Uh huh. And so that's at the end for whatever is not from faith faith, whatever does not come out of ourfulness to God is sin."],[2025.96,"By definition, it's disobedience"],[2032.34,"It's disloyalty. And so anything that we do that comes out of that, it doesn't matter if it's technically against the rules or not."],[2042.22,"If it comes out of that kind of spirit of disloyalty and disobedience, it's sin no matter what."],[2049.71,"Yeah. And that's that's helpful for the question I get asked most often by people in confession, which is, is this a sin?"],[2058.27,"And then they tell me something."],[2060.11,"And the answer is always very simple."],[2062.19,"It's if you have to ask, it is."],[2066.67,"It doesn't matter if there's a rule written down in a book somewhere."],[2067.39,"'s If it bothering you enough that you had to ask me, it was a sin."],[2075.91,"Uh-huh. It was a sin."],[2078.55,"Because it was not proceeding from faithfulness and trying to live a life because you were you were obsessing over this and concerned about this and divided from God by this."],[2091.27,"Yeah. Uh even if it was objectively speaking, really totally innocent."],[2097.8,"And if if you had done it out of your desire to live a life pleasing to God and serving God, you wouldn't have to ask."],[2106.3,"It would never occur to you."],[2107.82,"Uh-huh. So it must have come out of something else."],[2110.78,"Oh, that's very that's very helpful"],[2114.34,"Um so this is probably a good place to leave off and we'll finish up next week."],[2122.18,"Uh we've just got chapters fifteen and sixteen left."],[2125.54,"Chapter fifteen is a little longer and has a lot of great stuff in it."],[2129.22,"Most of uh chapter sixteen is say hi to so and so, say hi to so and so."],[2133.7,"Which is how pretty much all of St."],[2135.06,"Paul's letters end right along list there."],[2137.54,"Now that said, just like the genealogies in the old testament, people tend to brush through those pretty quickly."],[2144.66,"Um, and there are some things to note with some of the names."],[2147.46,"So we will talk about it and and go through a lot of um a lot of who was where yeah, but even the key to I've been I've been saying this whole time that uh St."],[2159.74,"Paul wrote the epistle to the Romans after the expulsion of the Jews by Claudius and when they came back, and the biggest piece of evidence for that being true is actually in chapter 16 in that list of names."],[2173.34,"So, but we'll we'll uh there's a teaser."],[2176.54,"We'll uh we'll talk about that next week when we finish up Romans."],[2180.54,"So thank you."],[2181.98,"Thank you. Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2190.7,"Father Stephen's email address is whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2195.98,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":22.96,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:1 - Receive the weak in faith","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:1</b>: receive one <b>weak in the faith</b>, but <b>not to disputes over doubtful things</b></li><li class=\"d0\">All at <b>different stages</b>; besides physical age, a <b>spiritual maturity</b> level</li><li class=\"d1\">some very old, not very advanced spiritually; some very young, very advanced</li><li class=\"d1\">the two are <b>disassociated</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Weak</b> = spiritually <b>immature</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Receive</b> them - don't push off because they don't understand, aren't on board, <b>ask too many questions</b></li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>not</b> to <b>argue about everything</b></li><li class=\"d1\">purpose of receiving = they <b>grow toward greater maturity and understanding</b></li></ul>"},{"t":100.38,"lv":3,"h":"Fathers and theological disputes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reading <b>fathers, ascetics</b>: <b>theological disputes</b> play very little role</li><li class=\"d0\">Even fathers in controversies focused on <b>key things</b>, a <b>crisis right now</b>, things at <b>the heart of salvation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Jesus isn't God\" cuts to the <b>heart of the gospel</b> - must answer</li><li class=\"d0\">Someone says <b>alligator</b> on a fast day counts as <b>fish</b> - not what fathers spend time on</li><li class=\"d1\">details of <b>fasting rules</b> = what <b>rabbis</b> spent time on, and <b>internet message boards</b></li><li class=\"d1\">those debating aren't the <b>most mature</b> in the church - <b>not the bishops</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So: receive them, but <b>not for that</b></li></ul>"},{"t":188.2,"lv":3,"h":"What \"weak in the faith\" means","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not someone <b>not believing hard enough</b> - \"doesn't make any sense anyway\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not someone who doesn't understand how the <b>Eucharist</b> works</li><li class=\"d0\">A person whose Christian life isn't <b>mature and robust</b> - still <b>figuring things out</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Constant problem: wants <b>all the answers before committing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">biggest reason a friend hasn't come into Orthodoxy - afraid of being asked to believe what she isn't convinced of <b>rationally</b></li><li class=\"d1\">works in the <b>Episcopal Church</b>; shouldn't be an issue in Orthodoxy</li><li class=\"d1\">challenges him on <b>theological minutiae</b> - usually \"<b>I don't know</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Says in <b>catechumen class</b>: only <b>one reason</b> to join the Orthodox Church</li><li class=\"d1\">you've come and discovered <b>Christ is here</b></li><li class=\"d1\">haven't had that → <b>keep looking until you find Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if Christ is here, then <b>obedience</b> kicks in - in <b>intellect</b> too: <b>intellectual humility</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't understand this, but that doesn't mean it isn't true\"</li><li class=\"d1\">unsure about the <b>Theotokos</b> - but <b>Christ is here</b>; \"I'll understand at some point\"</li></ul>"},{"t":350.62,"lv":3,"h":"\"I believe so that I may understand\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Quoting <b>Augustine</b>: <b>I believe so that I may understand</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Comment from the room: conversion was an <b>experience</b></li><li class=\"d1\">had thrown out ideas because they <b>didn't make sense</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now had to <b>accept them</b>; they'd make sense eventually</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>50 years</b> on: \"oh, now I understand that\" - plenty still <b>not understood</b>, but <b>committed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"I take on <b>obedience</b>\" - not just faith</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Humility</b> of \"I don't understand\" - doesn't mean it makes <b>no sense</b>; \"I just don't get it <b>yet</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":445.64,"lv":3,"h":"Why some discussions aren't worth having","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Some theological discussions with <b>non-Orthodox</b> - politely, <b>not worth having</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Example: <b>Protestant</b> friend wanted to discuss <b>closed communion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why Eucharist isn't given to <b>non-Orthodox</b></li><li class=\"d1\">would have to accept <b>all we believe and experience</b> about the Eucharist</li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>discrete point</b> - part of the whole <b>lived experience</b> of Eucharist, liturgy, Orthodox life</li><li class=\"d1\">can't <b>debate it from outside</b> to convince without all the rest</li></ul>"},{"t":517.31,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:2 - The one who eats and the one who doesn't","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:2</b>: one believes he may <b>eat all things</b>, the weak <b>eats only vegetables</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"very bad sentence\" - translators added a word or two, <b>didn't help</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Person who eats anything: <b>Jewish food rules don't apply</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not worried meat from the <b>meat market</b> was involved in <b>sacrifice</b> - not at the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">eats, <b>gives thanks</b> to God</li><li class=\"d0\">The other: newer in the faith - <b>only vegetables</b> like <b>Daniel and friends</b> in Babylon</li><li class=\"d1\">no meat <b>offered to idols</b>; maybe <b>former pagan</b> or <b>Jewish</b> holding on to traditions</li><li class=\"d0\">Vegetarian <b>seems the strong one</b> - disciplined</li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>weak = spiritual maturity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I can eat anything\" reflects understanding of <b>purpose of OT food laws</b>, <b>Christ taking uncleanness</b> from the physical world</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I don't want to follow rules\" - reached through understanding <b>material world, Christ, Torah, meat offered to idols</b></li><li class=\"d0\">New convert: \"some meat might be <b>offered to idols</b> - better eat none\"; \"why keep some Torah but not <b>kosher</b>? better keep kosher\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not</b> the weak person <b>causing disputes</b> or demanding all follow rules - different category</li><li class=\"d1\">this person decides for <b>themselves</b> - ties to <b>conscience</b> coming later</li></ul>"},{"t":725.77,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:3-4 - Who are you to judge?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:3</b>: eater <b>doesn't despise</b> non-eater; non-eater <b>doesn't judge</b> eater - <b>God has received him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">eater shouldn't say \"you <b>ignoramus</b>, little faith\"</li><li class=\"d1\">vegetarian shouldn't say \"did you see he bought <b>meat</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:4</b>: \"who are you to judge <b>another's servant</b>? To his own <b>master</b> he stands or falls\" - <b>God is able to make him stand</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Focus is on Paul's <b>reasoning</b>, not on \"it's okay to watch this <b>TV show</b>... tell them to shut up\"</li><li class=\"d1\">both are <b>servants of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">two slaves, two employees: not their job to <b>evaluate each other's performance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>master / boss</b> evaluates</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ</b> will evaluate both - he's <b>not interested in your opinions</b> of each other</li><li class=\"d0\">Focus on serving <b>as faithfully as you are able</b></li></ul>"},{"t":860.4,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:5-6 - Days and food to the Lord","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:5</b>: one esteems one day above another, another <b>every day alike</b> - each <b>fully convinced in his own mind</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Observing a <b>day</b> = the <b>Jewish Sabbath</b></li><li class=\"d1\">those who observe it: doing it <b>for the Lord</b> - a good thing</li><li class=\"d1\">one who doesn't still gives the day to the Lord, <b>differently</b> - theologically <b>fulfilled</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God evaluates</b> how well each honors him in their own way</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:6</b>: eater <b>gives thanks</b> → glory to God</li><li class=\"d0\">Non-eater not eating to be <b>obedient to God</b> → God <b>honors that</b></li></ul>"},{"t":943.98,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:7-9 - None lives to himself","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:7-8</b>: none lives or dies <b>to himself</b>; live or die <b>to the Lord</b> - <b>we are the Lord's</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"you gotta <b>serve somebody</b>\" (<b>Bob Dylan</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul gives <b>no other option</b> - writing to the church... \"I'm about to question that\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Theology sneaks back in</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:9</b>: Christ <b>died and rose and lived again</b> to be <b>Lord of both the dead and the living</b></li><li class=\"d1\">seems a weird argument - what's it got to do with anything?</li><li class=\"d1\">his flow: Christ's dying and rising made it so <b>no escaping serving the Lord</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1039.69,"lv":3,"h":"Lord of the dead - Genesis 3","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Before Christ died: who was <b>Lord of the dead</b>? <b>Satan, the devil</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Goes back to <b>Genesis 3</b>, read \"in a goofy way\" today</li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Kipling's Just So story</b> about how the snake lost its legs - <b>not at all</b> what it's about</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Thrown down to the ground\": Heb. <i>erets</i> often used for the <b>underworld</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"eat dust\": ancients knew <b>snakes don't eat dirt</b>; they'd seen them eat <b>frogs, mice, rats</b></li><li class=\"d1\">dust = what <b>Adam returns to</b> - same chapter</li><li class=\"d0\">The curse: devil <b>cast down into the underworld</b> as <b>Lord of the dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">his punishment: a <b>kingdom of ashes and dust</b> for trying to <b>usurp God's kingdom</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hebrews</b>: devil <b>held the power of death</b> - <b>past tense</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1127.49,"lv":3,"h":"Harrowing of Hades - Lord of living and dead","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Christ's death: the <b>harrowing of Hades</b> - <b>binds him</b>, takes his authority, <b>plunders</b> the people</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pascha</b> language: \"<b>not one dead remains in the graves</b>\" - not one in the devil's realm</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ returns to <b>judge the living and the dead</b> - <b>everyone now under his authority</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Everyone who's ever lived: Christ is <b>Lord and Master</b></li><li class=\"d1\">whether they <b>acknowledge or believe</b> it now, they'll <b>give account</b> at judgment</li><li class=\"d0\">Extends to <b>every human being</b> you meet, ever</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>preaching the gospel</b> = telling them: Christ <b>died, rose, ascended, sits enthroned</b>, returning to judge</li><li class=\"d1\">so they can <b>live in relationship</b> to that fact - \"<b>we don't get to vote</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1238.16,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:10-12 - The judgment seat of Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:10</b>: why <b>judge your brother</b> or show contempt? <b>all stand before the judgment seat of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">each gives account <b>to him</b> - not to me, and I'm not accountable to you</li><li class=\"d1\">both account for <b>words, deeds, thoughts</b> to Christ, our master</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:11</b>: <b>Isaiah 45:23</b> - \"as I live, says the Lord, every knee shall bow to me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Lord\" in all caps = <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:12</b>: each gives <b>account of himself to God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Prophetic of <b>that day</b> - all will acknowledge Christ as Lord whether they wanted to or not</li><li class=\"d1\">then revealed <b>what kind of servant</b> we were</li></ul>"},{"t":1286.84,"lv":3,"h":"Philippians 2 - Christ is Yahweh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Similar in <b>Philippians 2:10-11</b>: every knee shall bow, every tongue confess <b>Jesus Christ is Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>repurposes</b> the Isaiah text → <b>Jesus Christ is Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">clearer: \"to the <b>glory of God the Father</b>\" - Christ hasn't <b>displaced</b> the Father; the two are <b>one</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Yet another place\" where Paul makes it clear <b>Christ is Yahweh</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1400.23,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:13 - No stumbling block","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:13</b>: no more judging; <b>resolve not to put a stumbling block</b> in a brother's way</li><li class=\"d0\">Speaks <b>practically</b> now about showing <b>love</b> to the brother</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>negative</b>: not judging, evaluating, condemning</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>positive alternative</b>: <b>not putting a stumbling block</b> or cause to fall</li><li class=\"d1\">= not leading him into <b>temptation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He'll stand before Christ; I serve Christ → <b>my job to help him serve Christ better</b></li><li class=\"d1\">by helping him serve Christ, <b>I'm serving Christ</b> - the two go together</li></ul>"},{"t":1464.31,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:14-15 - Do not destroy with your food","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:14</b>: Paul is <b>convinced by the Lord Jesus</b>: <b>nothing unclean of itself</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ <b>cleansed and purified the material world</b> (back in <b>Acts</b>) - no unclean foods</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul now in the position of the <b>mature one</b></li><li class=\"d0\">But to him who <b>considers it unclean</b>, it is unclean</li><li class=\"d1\">honestly believes eating = <b>sin against God</b> → acting against it is <b>sin because of his attitude</b>, <b>in his heart</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:15</b>: brother <b>grieved because of your food</b> = <b>no longer walking in love</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>do not destroy with your food the one for whom Christ died</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Example: <b>local Chinese restaurant</b>, no worry about <b>incense</b> while cooking; could eat <b>pork</b>, give thanks</li><li class=\"d1\">but someone sees me, \"I guess he <b>gets away with it</b>, so I can\" → <b>follows my example</b></li><li class=\"d1\">breaks his <b>conscience</b> on that, then <b>other things</b> we'd all agree are wrong</li><li class=\"d1\">moves from <b>trying to be obedient</b> to <b>not caring</b>, more <b>lax</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ <b>died</b> for this person - \"you don't care enough to not eat a <b>ham sandwich</b>, get <b>roast beef</b> instead\"</li><li class=\"d1\">minimal definition of <b>love and compassion</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1648.39,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:16-18 - Kingdom of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:16</b>: don't let your good be <b>spoken of as evil</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:17</b>: kingdom of God <b>not eating and drinking</b> but <b>righteousness, peace, joy in the Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>these</b> are what we're after - not eating, drinking, <b>having a good time</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:18</b>: he who serves Christ in these = <b>acceptable to God, approved by men</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1672.41,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:19-21 - Pursue peace and edify","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:19</b>: pursue <b>things which make for peace</b>, edify one another</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:20-21</b>: don't <b>destroy the work of God</b> for food</li><li class=\"d1\">all things pure, but <b>evil for the man who eats with offense</b></li><li class=\"d1\">good <b>neither to eat meat nor drink wine</b> nor anything by which your brother <b>stumbles</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wine</b> = a better modern example</li><li class=\"d1\">I may enjoy an <b>adult beverage</b> now and then, no issue; <b>plenty can't</b></li><li class=\"d1\">seen especially as <b>clergy</b> → leads them wrong → \"I can drink a <b>Diet Coke</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">out with <b>Baptists</b>: don't order a <b>martini</b></li><li class=\"d0\">About <b>love</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1746.63,"lv":3,"h":"Asceticism and love vs. rights","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul already clear: no <b>provision for sinful desires</b></li><li class=\"d1\">here even <b>non-sinful desires</b> sacrificed for <b>better things</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Basis of <b>asceticism</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not giving up <b>sin</b> - always supposed to</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>giving up good things to get better things</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Lent</b>: no chicken, full belly, <b>entertainment spending</b> - to focus on what's <b>more important</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same thing Paul argues <b>all the time</b>, out of love in the community</li><li class=\"d0\">Question isn't \"is this a <b>sin</b>, technically?\" - back to <b>rules vs. love</b></li><li class=\"d1\">question: <b>is this showing love</b> for my neighbor?</li><li class=\"d1\">could be yes: in someone's <b>home</b>, sharing a drink = <b>fellowship, brotherhood in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not in the home of a <b>recovering alcoholic</b>; not <b>cracking open a beer</b> in the youth group</li><li class=\"d0\">Called to give up <b>freedoms and rights</b> out of love</li><li class=\"d1\">Americans: \"I have the <b>right</b> to this and that, you can't tell me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul charts the <b>opposite course</b>: responsible for <b>doing good, loving, peace</b></li><li class=\"d1\">more important than my rights → giving them up is <b>a good trade</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1912.83,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 14:22-23 - Whatever is not from faith","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:22</b>: \"do you have faith? <b>Have it to yourself before God</b>\" - happy is he who <b>doesn't condemn himself</b> in what he approves</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>mature</b>: know things are fine, can do them in <b>moderation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">you'll have things to <b>enjoy</b> that the weaker can't yet do <b>responsibly</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>14:23</b>: he who <b>doubts is condemned</b> if he eats - <b>not from faith</b></li><li class=\"d1\">thinks it's wrong, <b>does it anyway</b> → \"you know you're a <b>sinner</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>faith</b> can be translated <b>faithfulness</b> - not eating out of <b>obedience</b> to God, <b>quite the opposite</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Whatever is not from faith is sin</b>\" = <b>disloyalty, disobedience</b> by definition</li><li class=\"d1\">sin <b>no matter what</b> if from that spirit - even if not technically against the rules</li></ul>"},{"t":2049.71,"lv":3,"h":"\"Is this a sin?\" - if you have to ask","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Most common question in <b>confession</b>: \"<b>is this a sin?</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">answer always: \"<b>if you have to ask, it is</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not about a rule in a book</li><li class=\"d1\">bothering you enough to ask = <b>not proceeding from faithfulness</b>; <b>obsessing, divided from God</b> over it</li><li class=\"d1\">sin <b>even if objectively innocent</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Done from desire to <b>live pleasing to God</b>, you wouldn't have to ask - <b>never occur to you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q's reaction: \"very helpful\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2114.34,"lv":2,"h":"Wrapping up - what's left","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Leave off here; <b>finish next week</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Left: chapters <b>15 and 16</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ch. 15</b> a little longer, <b>lots of great stuff</b></li><li class=\"d1\">most of <b>ch. 16</b> = \"<b>say hi to so and so</b>\" - how nearly all of Paul's letters end</li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>OT genealogies</b>, people brush through - but <b>things to note</b> in some names</li><li class=\"d0\">Teaser: Romans written after <b>Claudius's expulsion of the Jews</b> and their return</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>biggest evidence</b> for that is in the <b>names in ch. 16</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Romans 15-16</b> - finish up Romans"});
